-- title:
--   Surjection onto a free algebra with small kernel is injective
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative local ring, let $A$ be a commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra which is local and Noetherian and whose structure morphism $\mathcal{O}\to A$ is a local homomorphism (it carries the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$ into that of $A$), and let $B$ be a commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra which is free as an $\mathcal{O}$-module. Let $f\colon A\to B$ be a homomorphism of $\mathcal{O}$-algebras which is surjective as a map of sets, and assume that the kernel ideal of $f$ is contained in the ideal $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}A$ of $A$, that is, in the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$ under the structure map $\mathcal{O}\to A$. Then $f$ is injective, hence an isomorphism of $\mathcal{O}$-algebras onto $B$. Neither finiteness of $B$ as an $\mathcal{O}$-module nor completeness of any of the rings is assumed; $B$ is not assumed local.
--
--   This is the Nakayama step in the de Smit–Rubin–Schoof treatment of the Wiles–Lenstra numerical criterion for complete intersections: it upgrades surjectivity together with control of the kernel modulo $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$ to bijectivity for maps onto an $\mathcal{O}$-free algebra of the Hecke type. It is used here by [`AlgHom.bijective_and_exists_presentation_of_length_cotangent_le`](thm.html#AlgHom.bijective_and_exists_presentation_of_length_cotangent_le) and by [`Algebra.exists_presentation_of_residueField`](thm.html#Algebra.exists_presentation_of_residueField).
